{"route":"/docs/5.2/layout/breakpoints/","version":"5.2","renderedVersion":"5.2","title":{"id":"content","type":"heading","en":"Breakpoints","level":1},"lead":{"id":"content--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Breakpoints are customizable widths that determine how your responsive layout behaves across device or viewport sizes in Bootstrap."},"blocks":[{"id":"core-concepts","type":"heading","en":"Core concepts","level":2},{"id":"core-concepts--list-1","type":"list","tag":"ul","items":[{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"core-concepts--item-1","type":"item","en":"<strong>Breakpoints are the building blocks of responsive design.</strong> Use them to control when your layout can be adapted at a particular viewport or device size."}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"core-concepts--item-2","type":"item","en":"<strong>Use media queries to architect your CSS by breakpoint.</strong> Media queries are a feature of CSS that allow you to conditionally apply styles based on a set of browser and operating system parameters. We most commonly use <code>min-width</code> in our media queries."}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"core-concepts--item-3","type":"item","en":"<strong>Mobile first, responsive design is the goal.</strong> Bootstrap’s CSS aims to apply the bare minimum of styles to make a layout work at the smallest breakpoint, and then layers on styles to adjust that design for larger devices. This optimizes your CSS, improves rendering time, and provides a great experience for your visitors."}]}]},{"id":"available-breakpoints","type":"heading","en":"Available breakpoints","level":2},{"id":"available-breakpoints--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Bootstrap includes six default breakpoints, sometimes referred to as <em>grid tiers</em>, for building responsively. These breakpoints can be customized if you’re using our source Sass files."},{"id":"available-breakpoints--table-1","type":"table","caption":[],"rows":[{"head":true,"cells":[{"type":"th","body":[{"id":"available-breakpoints--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Breakpoint"}]},{"type":"th","body":[{"id":"available-breakpoints--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"Class infix"}]},{"type":"th","body":[{"id":"available-breakpoints--paragraph-4","type":"paragraph","en":"Dimensions"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"available-breakpoints--paragraph-5","type":"paragraph","en":"Extra small"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"available-breakpoints--paragraph-6","type":"paragraph","en":"<em>None</em>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"available-breakpoints--paragraph-7","type":"paragraph","en":"&lt;576px"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"available-breakpoints--paragraph-8","type":"paragraph","en":"Small"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"available-breakpoints--paragraph-9","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>sm</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"available-breakpoints--paragraph-10","type":"paragraph","en":"≥576px"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"available-breakpoints--paragraph-11","type":"paragraph","en":"Medium"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"available-breakpoints--paragraph-12","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>md</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"available-breakpoints--paragraph-13","type":"paragraph","en":"≥768px"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"available-breakpoints--paragraph-14","type":"paragraph","en":"Large"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"available-breakpoints--paragraph-15","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>lg</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"available-breakpoints--paragraph-16","type":"paragraph","en":"≥992px"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"available-breakpoints--paragraph-17","type":"paragraph","en":"Extra large"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"available-breakpoints--paragraph-18","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>xl</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"available-breakpoints--paragraph-19","type":"paragraph","en":"≥1200px"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"available-breakpoints--paragraph-20","type":"paragraph","en":"Extra extra large"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"available-breakpoints--paragraph-21","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>xxl</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"available-breakpoints--paragraph-22","type":"paragraph","en":"≥1400px"}]}]}]},{"id":"available-breakpoints--paragraph-23","type":"paragraph","en":"Each breakpoint was chosen to comfortably hold containers whose widths are multiples of 12. Breakpoints are also representative of a subset of common device sizes and viewport dimensions—they don’t specifically target every use case or device. Instead, the ranges provide a strong and consistent foundation to build on for nearly any device."},{"id":"available-breakpoints--paragraph-24","type":"paragraph","en":"These breakpoints are customizable via Sass—you’ll find them in a Sass map in our <code>_variables.scss</code> stylesheet."},{"id":"available-breakpoints--code-1","type":"code","value":"$grid-breakpoints: (\n  xs: 0,\n  sm: 576px,\n  md: 768px,\n  lg: 992px,\n  xl: 1200px,\n  xxl: 1400px\n);","language":"scss"},{"id":"available-breakpoints--paragraph-25","type":"paragraph","en":"For more information and examples on how to modify our Sass maps and variables, please refer to <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/layout/grid/#sass\">the Sass section of the Grid documentation</a>."},{"id":"media-queries","type":"heading","en":"Media queries","level":2},{"id":"media-queries--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Since Bootstrap is developed to be mobile first, we use a handful of <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Media_Queries/Using_media_queries\">media queries</a> to create sensible breakpoints for our layouts and interfaces. These breakpoints are mostly based on minimum viewport widths and allow us to scale up elements as the viewport changes."},{"id":"min-width","type":"heading","en":"Min-width","level":3},{"id":"min-width--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Bootstrap primarily uses the following media query ranges—or breakpoints—in our source Sass files for our layout, grid system, and components."},{"id":"min-width--code-1","type":"code","value":"// Source mixins\n\n// No media query necessary for xs breakpoint as it's effectively `@media (min-width: 0) { ... }`\n@include media-breakpoint-up(sm) { ... }\n@include media-breakpoint-up(md) { ... }\n@include media-breakpoint-up(lg) { ... }\n@include media-breakpoint-up(xl) { ... }\n@include media-breakpoint-up(xxl) { ... }\n\n// Usage\n\n// Example: Hide starting at `min-width: 0`, and then show at the `sm` breakpoint\n.custom-class {\n  display: none;\n}\n@include media-breakpoint-up(sm) {\n  .custom-class {\n    display: block;\n  }\n}","language":"scss"},{"id":"min-width--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"These Sass mixins translate in our compiled CSS using the values declared in our Sass variables. For example:"},{"id":"min-width--code-2","type":"code","value":"// X-Small devices (portrait phones, less than 576px)\n// No media query for `xs` since this is the default in Bootstrap\n\n// Small devices (landscape phones, 576px and up)\n@media (min-width: 576px) { ... }\n\n// Medium devices (tablets, 768px and up)\n@media (min-width: 768px) { ... }\n\n// Large devices (desktops, 992px and up)\n@media (min-width: 992px) { ... }\n\n// X-Large devices (large desktops, 1200px and up)\n@media (min-width: 1200px) { ... }\n\n// XX-Large devices (larger desktops, 1400px and up)\n@media (min-width: 1400px) { ... }","language":"scss"},{"id":"max-width","type":"heading","en":"Max-width","level":3},{"id":"max-width--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"We occasionally use media queries that go in the other direction (the given screen size <em>or smaller</em>):"},{"id":"max-width--code-1","type":"code","value":"// No media query necessary for xs breakpoint as it's effectively `@media (max-width: 0) { ... }`\n@include media-breakpoint-down(sm) { ... }\n@include media-breakpoint-down(md) { ... }\n@include media-breakpoint-down(lg) { ... }\n@include media-breakpoint-down(xl) { ... }\n@include media-breakpoint-down(xxl) { ... }\n\n// Example: Style from medium breakpoint and down\n@include media-breakpoint-down(md) {\n  .custom-class {\n    display: block;\n  }\n}","language":"scss"},{"id":"max-width--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"These mixins take those declared breakpoints, subtract <code>.02px</code> from them, and use them as our <code>max-width</code> values. For example:"},{"id":"max-width--code-2","type":"code","value":"// `xs` returns only a ruleset and no media query\n// ... { ... }\n\n// `sm` applies to x-small devices (portrait phones, less than 576px)\n@media (max-width: 575.98px) { ... }\n\n// `md` applies to small devices (landscape phones, less than 768px)\n@media (max-width: 767.98px) { ... }\n\n// `lg` applies to medium devices (tablets, less than 992px)\n@media (max-width: 991.98px) { ... }\n\n// `xl` applies to large devices (desktops, less than 1200px)\n@media (max-width: 1199.98px) { ... }\n\n// `xxl` applies to x-large devices (large desktops, less than 1400px)\n@media (max-width: 1399.98px) { ... }","language":"scss"},{"id":"max-width--note-1","type":"note","tone":"warning","body":[{"id":"max-width--note-text-1","type":"note-text","en":"<strong>Why subtract .02px?</strong> Browsers don’t currently support <a href=\"https://www.w3.org/TR/mediaqueries-4/#range-context\">range context queries</a>, so we work around the limitations of <a href=\"https://www.w3.org/TR/mediaqueries-4/#mq-min-max\"><code>min-</code> and <code>max-</code> prefixes</a> and viewports with fractional widths (which can occur under certain conditions on high-dpi devices, for instance) by using values with higher precision."}]},{"id":"single-breakpoint","type":"heading","en":"Single breakpoint","level":3},{"id":"single-breakpoint--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"There are also media queries and mixins for targeting a single segment of screen sizes using the minimum and maximum breakpoint widths."},{"id":"single-breakpoint--code-1","type":"code","value":"@include media-breakpoint-only(xs) { ... }\n@include media-breakpoint-only(sm) { ... }\n@include media-breakpoint-only(md) { ... }\n@include media-breakpoint-only(lg) { ... }\n@include media-breakpoint-only(xl) { ... }\n@include media-breakpoint-only(xxl) { ... }","language":"scss"},{"id":"single-breakpoint--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"For example the <code>@include media-breakpoint-only(md) { ... }</code> will result in :"},{"id":"single-breakpoint--code-2","type":"code","value":"@media (min-width: 768px) and (max-width: 991.98px) { ... }","language":"scss"},{"id":"between-breakpoints","type":"heading","en":"Between breakpoints","level":3},{"id":"between-breakpoints--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Similarly, media queries may span multiple breakpoint widths:"},{"id":"between-breakpoints--code-1","type":"code","value":"@include media-breakpoint-between(md, xl) { ... }","language":"scss"},{"id":"between-breakpoints--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Which results in:"},{"id":"between-breakpoints--code-2","type":"code","value":"// Example\n// Apply styles starting from medium devices and up to extra large devices\n@media (min-width: 768px) and (max-width: 1199.98px) { ... }","language":"scss"}],"demos":[],"nav":[{"en":"Introduction","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/getting-started/introduction/"},{"en":"Download","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/getting-started/download/"},{"en":"Contents","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/getting-started/contents/"},{"en":"Browsers & devices","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/getting-started/browsers-devices/"},{"en":"JavaScript","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/getting-started/javascript/"},{"en":"Webpack","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/getting-started/webpack/"},{"en":"Parcel","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/getting-started/parcel/"},{"en